      ":question/id": "957ed435-c537-593e-a6aa-bb7c0527f0e4",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
      ":question/problem": "Express $\\cos^2\\left(140^\\circ\\right)-\\sin^2\\left(140^\\circ\\right)$ as a single trigonometric ratio.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Use the cosine double-angle formula:\n\n$$\n\\cos^2 x-\\sin^2 x=\\cos(2x)\n$$\n\nSubstitute $x=140^\\circ$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\cos^2\\left(140^\\circ\\right)-\\sin^2\\left(140^\\circ\\right)&=\\cos\\left(2\\cdot 140^\\circ\\right)\\\\&=\\cos\\left(280^\\circ\\right)\n\\end{aligned}\n$$",
